libzpaq.cpp (LIBZPAQ 7.15, 2016-08-17) and libzpaq.h (header 7.12) from
https://github.com/zpaq/zpaq, commit 9ab539f644e364f0d92e2918b90ce2534c75653f,
fetched 2026-10-30, byte-identical: md5 a7c5eee984d195b5dd66fc2a933449b3
and 9a67677ddd41c774664aaa2ade363a58. Matt Mahoney released both into the
public domain; the libdivsufsort inside libzpaq.cpp is MIT (see its comments).

kzzpaq.cpp is karyozip's: it cuts nothing itself, it compresses the pieces
the caller gives with libzpaq::compressBlock(method "5", no SHA-1) side by
side under OpenMP, and writes the piece count, then each piece's size and
its zpaq block's size (u32 little endian), then the blocks. libzpaq.cpp is
built without OpenMP, since its divsufsort spawns its own threads, with
-Dunix, and with -DNOJIT off x86-64; JIT and interpreter give the same bytes.
